    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, led by **Brice Turang** (75.06) and **Corbin Carroll** (73.47). **Brice Turang** is our strongest play, bolstered by a juicy matchup against Merrill Kelly, whose 5.47 xERA provides an ideal environment for **Brice Turang** to capitalize on his elite speed-based scoring floor. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** remains a top-tier asset today; despite facing a capable arm in Brandon Woodruff, the combination of the favorable park factor and a slow pitcher delivery profile significantly inflates his stolen base probability, keeping his daily efficiency well into the elite range. **Josh Naylor** (70.49) also demands attention, as his matchup against a struggling Bieber (5.52 xERA) presents a prime opportunity to drive in runs and bolster our RBI totals, assuming he maintains his middle-of-the-order protection.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today\u2019s roster construction centered on **Alex Freeland**, who finished at 49.35\u2014just barely missing the cut behind **Austin Riley** (49.38). While **Alex Freeland** offers switch-hitting versatility, the optimizer favored the sheer volume of plate appearances and situational floor provided by **Austin Riley**, despite the latter\u2019s tough draw against Sean Manaea. Meanwhile, we are exercising caution with several \"Lineup Pending\" designations; specifically, **Mickey Moniak** (69.94) and **Kyle Karros** (63.20) are currently slotted to face Robbie Ray, and while the park factors are favorable, both could see their efficiency numbers swing significantly depending on official lineup placement. \n\nWe are monitoring risk closely with **Gabriel Moreno**, whose score of 55.77 is respectable but shadowed by the threat of Brandon Woodruff\u2019s moderate 3.83 xERA. While **James Wood** (51.23) currently occupies our OF5 spot, his elite 0.418 xwOBA is being suppressed by a tough matchup against Hunter Ashcraft; we are keeping him in the lineup strictly for his high-end peripheral upside, even if his current efficiency score is lower than some of our other rostered options. We remain lean and aggressive on the basepaths, trusting our speed-weighted selections to navigate the volatility of today\u2019s pitcher-heavy matchups.",
